<title>INDIA: India RBI interest caps for forex deposits.</title>
<headline>India RBI interest caps for forex deposits.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Tuesday prescribed the following ceilings on interest rates on foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>Earlier on Tuesday, the RBI said in its credit and monetary policy for first half 1997/98 (April-March) that banks could determine interest rates subject to the ceiling.</p>
<p>							(percent per annum)</p>
<p>Maturity				    GBP     USD     DM     JPY</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>6 months and above but less than</p>
<p>one year				    5.25    4.50   2.75   0.50</p>
<p>One year and above but less than</p>
<p>two years				   6.25    5.75   3.50   0.75</p>
<p>Two years and above but less than</p>
<p>three years				 6.75    6.00   4.25   1.00</p>
<p>Three years only			  7.00    6.25   4.75   1.50</p>
<p>Note.  GBP - pound sterling</p>
<p>	 USD - dollar</p>
<p>	 DM  - deutschemark</p>
<p>	 JPY - Japanese yen</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The RBI said the ceiling rates would be revised as and when required.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom</p>
</text>
